---
source: src/cli/cli_args.rs
expression: output
---
mount-luks x.y.z
Unlock and mount LUKS encrypted disks

Usage: mount-luks [--config <CONFIG>] [--log-level <LOG_LEVEL>] [SUBCOMMAND]

Commands:
  mount     Unlock and mount a LUKS encrypted partition
  set-luks  Add the passphrase to LUKS
  set-tpm   Seal the passphrase component in the TPM
  validate  Validate the LUKS passphrase without unlocking
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Flags:
      --config <CONFIG>        Path to a specific config file
      --log-level <LOG_LEVEL>  Set the log level
                               [possible values: error, warn, info, debug,
                               trace]
  -h, --help                   Print help
  -V, --version                Print version
